---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
const lastUpdated = "August 1, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description={`${siteConfig.name}'s privacy policy: what data is collected, how it's used, and which third-party services are involved.`}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} is a small, independently-run technical blog. This policy
      explains what happens when you read it.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site collects today</h2>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} uses Google Analytics to understand which posts are actually
      useful — but only if you say yes. On your first visit, a banner asks for your
      consent before anything loads; if you decline or don't respond, no analytics
      script runs and no analytics cookie is set. You can change your answer any time
      via "Cookie preferences" in the footer. If you accept, Google Analytics sets
      cookies on your device and processes standard usage data (pages viewed, approximate
      location from IP, device/browser type, referring site) under{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">
        Google's own privacy policy
      </a>. Reading the site does not create an account or any stored profile of
      you beyond that. Server logs at the hosting layer (Cloudflare) may record
      standard technical data — IP address, user agent, requested URL, timestamp
      — the same way any web server does;{" "}
      {siteConfig.name} does not access or process these logs beyond normal operational
      troubleshooting.
    </p>

    <h2>What may be added later, and how it will be handled</h2>
    <p>
      If comments are added (via Giscus, which authenticates through your own
      GitHub account), that exchange happens directly between you and GitHub; {
        siteConfig.name
      } does not see or store your GitHub credentials. If advertising, affiliate links,
      or a newsletter are ever added, this page will be updated first, and any additional
      tracking that requires consent will be gated behind an actual consent prompt,
      not just a mention on this page. See the{" "}
      <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate/Advertising Disclosure</a>{" "}
      page for the current status of monetization on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      Posts on {siteConfig.name} link out to external tools, documentation, and services.
      Once you follow an outbound link, that site's own privacy practices apply —
      this policy only covers {siteConfig.name}{" "}
      itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can decline Google Analytics entirely — see "What this site collects
      today" above — and nothing described there will apply to you. If you
      already accepted and want to withdraw, use "Cookie preferences" in the
      footer to change your answer, or clear your browser's local storage and
      cookies for this site directly. For anything else — a question about
      what's collected, or a request related to it — reach out via the{" "}
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} is operated from {siteConfig.jurisdiction}, and this
      policy is governed by the laws of {siteConfig.jurisdiction}. If you're
      located elsewhere and local law grants you additional data rights, this
      site's practices above still apply — reach out via the{" "}
      <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page with any request and it will be handled
      directly, rather than pointing you to a formal process that doesn't exist yet
      for a site this size.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This page will be updated whenever what {siteConfig.name} collects or how it's
      handled changes — the "Last updated" date above reflects the most recent revision.
    </p>

    <p class="legal__disclaimer">
      This page is provided for transparency and is not a substitute for legal
      advice.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .legal__updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * -2);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 6);
  }

  .legal__disclaimer {
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 8);
    padding-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
</style>
